    "narrative": "With limited action on today\u2019s slate, the Zurich Zebras\u2019 offensive production centers on a pair of mid-tier starts against Henderson and Rasmussen. **Christian Yelich** earns the highest score of the day at 55.03, buoyed by an advantageous platoon matchup against Rasmussen. While the opposing starter\u2019s 3.30 xERA limits the ceiling, **Christian Yelich** benefits significantly from his #3 spot in the lineup, providing a stable floor for our R/RBI targets. **Junior Caminero** follows closely at 52.05; despite a tougher draw against Henderson, **Junior Caminero** remains a daily staple because his recent form is peaking at 100% of his projection. Neither play hits the \"Strong\" threshold, reflecting a day where we must prioritize game-cap preservation over aggressive streaming.\n\nThe depth of our bench is entirely neutralized today as **Yordan Alvarez**, **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Caleb Durbin** are all inactive. The absence of **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is particularly painful given our mandate to prioritize stolen base threats, as their elite sprint speed would have been an automatic anchor for the lineup if they were on the field. Without those burners available, we are forced to rely on the current configuration of **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Carson Benge**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, all of whom are effectively benched to avoid wasted utilization. We are monitoring the lineups for potential late-game pinch-hit opportunities for **Lars Nootbaar** or **Josh Smith** should the game flow demand an aggressive pinch-hit maneuver, but for now, we remain committed to a conservative roster management strategy.",
